COLLEGE PARK, Md. — University of Maryland President Wallace Loh on Tuesday apologized for his role in the decision to invite former Secretary of Defense Robert Gates to give a speech at the university, despite his comments about African American athletes in college sports.
Speaking to reporters, Loh acknowledged that his decision to invite Gates was "a mistake" and that he should have been more mindful of the potential impact of Gates' comments
